\section{How the code is read}{

The expression is captured with \code{\link[=substitute]{substitute()}} and turned back into text
with \code{\link[=deparse]{deparse()}}. This means comments are dropped and the code is
re-formatted in R's standard style. Line numbers in the report refer to
this normalised code, which is stored in the \code{original} element of the
result. To analyse a script with its comments and original line numbers,
use \code{\link[=nitro_file]{nitro_file()}}.
